 "notes": [
  "The offer that appears once a session at a calm moment (client/scenes/court/offer_popup.gd, layout client/layout/offer_popup.json), cut from art/reference/offers_popup.png. The painting's background (a dimmed castle) stands for the game behind it and is not cut: the plate is cut by its own outline -- the plate, the crimson banner, the two fleurs and the close button, a union of the plate's chamfered outline, the close button's circle, and the banner and fleurs traced off their own warm gold and crimson (so no wedge of the castle behind their curls comes with them) -- and the game's own screen shows dimmed behind it.",
  "Its banner, tiles, timer plate and green button are painted empty: the offer's title, what it holds, how long it lasts and its App Store price are set live. LATER keeps its painted word. The pack painting keeps its BEST VALUE ribbon: every offer the catalogue fires beats the diamond packs at its price (the cheapest pays 75 a dollar with two potions, against the packs' 61 to 85).",
